WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:06.260
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:14.660
The reading from the Sinaxadion for October 6 on which we commemorate the Holy Apostle

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:24.870
Thomas, on the 6th of the month we celebrate the memory of the Holy Apostle Thomas.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:31.630
The Holy Apostle Thomas, also called Dittamus, was born in Judea.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:38.590
His parents were poor but they passed on to him a great love for the Law of Moses.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:44.870
When he was still young, he drew apart from the noisy games of his companions to devote

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:49.790
himself to reading and meditating upon the scriptures.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:56.190
His knowledge of God's word and will disposed conscience enabled him without hesitation

00:00:56.270 --> 00:01:02.990
to recognize Christ as the Messiah, spoken of by the prophets, and to follow him as

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:05.510
soon as he called him.

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:10.870
He left his boat and his nets and became one of the twelve.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:18.230
He was persecuted, excluded and stoned by the Jews, yet followed the Savior everywhere

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:24.750
with such burning zeal that when Christ took the road for Jerusalem to offer himself

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:28.230
for those who were going to kill him.

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:38.070
Thomas said to the other disciples, let us also go that we may die with him.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:43.190
When the Savior of the world had overcome death by rising from the tomb, he appeared to his

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:48.870
disciples who were assembled with the doors shut for fear of the Jews.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:55.710
He showed them the marks of his passion upon his body and the disciples were filled with joy.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:02:01.710
God so provided that Thomas was not then with them, and when the others told him that

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:07.350
they had seen the Lord risen from the dead, he was unwilling to believe them.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:13.750
In his great patience and forbearance, the Lord appeared again to his disciples a week

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:21.230
later, and asked Thomas to certify that he was well and truly risen from the dead in

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:22.710
the flesh.

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:30.070
He told him to put his finger into the holes in his hands, left by the nails, and to thrust

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:36.820
his hand into his side pierced by the spear.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:43.500
In admonishing Thomas for his lack of faith, the Savior showed that we too are called upon

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:52.220
to thrust our hands into his side, not physically, but spiritually, to quench our thirst there

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:55.740
at the wellspring of grace.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:01.900
Thomas was with the other apostles when on the day of Pentecost the Holy Spirit came down

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:06.260
upon their heads in the form of tongues of fire.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:12.500
He was filled like the rest with power from on high for the proclamation of the world's

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:20.420
salvation, and when the Holy Apostles went their separate ways, it fell to Thomas to bring

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:31.660
the glad tidings to the distant lands of the Meads and Parthians, Iran, and as far as India.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:39.900
At that time there was in Jerusalem a man called Ambanas sent by an Indian king to find

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:46.580
an architect with skill enough to build him a palace that should surpass in beauty and

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:52.540
adornment any constructed by previous master builders.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:59.580
Made known to Thomas that this was the providential means for him to fulfill his mission, so he

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:06.540
made out to Ambanas that he was a slave, expert in the builder's art.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:13.580
They took ship for India, therefore, and arrived at the court of King Gundafar.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:19.340
The king was enraptured by the plan of the magnificent palace that Thomas laid before

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:25.740
him, and left him with a large sum of money for building it, before leaving for a three-year

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:29.340
tour of some distant provinces.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:34.980
As soon as he had charge of these riches, Thomas did not delay in distributing them to

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:42.540
the countless poor, starving Fulcum the king and his nobles had taken no care for at all.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:48.300
As well as relieving the poor, the apostle worked miracles and preached the gospel to

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:53.940
such good effect that a great many pagans were brought to the faith.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:59.300
When the king sent to know how the building works were getting on, Thomas asked him for more

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:04.060
gold on the pretext of finishing the roof.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:10.500
The king was delighted and immediately sent what he asked for, and it never entered his

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:17.220
head that Thomas was giving it away as soon as he received it.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:23.820
All the more terrible was his wrath then, when he found out that he had been tricked, and

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:28.300
that the saint had given all his money to the poor.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:34.140
Thomas was shot up in a deep pit, and the king had the most dreadful torments in store

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:35.140
for him.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:43.140
But that very night, his brother, who was grievously sick, had a vision of an angel who

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:50.580
carried him away and showed him a magnificent palace in the everlasting kingdom of the righteous.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:58.280
The angel said to him, Behold, the palace prepared for your brother, built for him by the

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:01.180
apostle Thomas.

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:06.700
When he came to himself, he described all he had seen to the king, and how much more

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:13.820
beautiful than any earthly dwelling was the palace Thomas had built for him in heaven.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:20.660
Completely overwhelmed, the king repented, released the apostle, and asked for baptism with

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:22.860
his brother.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:29.500
St. Thomas then left for another kingdom, where barbarity and godlessness held sway with

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:32.020
yet more violence.

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:40.020
But in the power of the Holy Spirit, he succeeded in converting Tersia, the king's wife, her son

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:45.660
Azzanas and her two daughters, Megzonia and Marza.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:53.380
He baptized them and taught them how to follow the way of perfection in Askees and Chastity.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:07:00.580
This seemed a peculiar and senseless way of life to the lustful king, and it threw him

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:02.460
into a rage.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:09.980
He had St. Thomas seized and ordered five soldiers to spear him through on a mountain, outside

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:17.620
the city, so it was that the apostle departed to rejoice forever with the Lord.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:23.870
He is venerated as the founder of the church in India.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:30.830
Through the prayers of our Holy Father's O Lord, Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:31.990
and save us.
